t not satisfied; S has only 6 electrons. (d) Methylamine, as drawn: the nitrogen is bonded to the carbon and to three H, with no lone pair. Corrected: CH3NH2, nitrogen bonded to carbon and two H with one lone pair. Error: four bonds and no lone pair is the pattern of a positive nitrogen, as in CH3NH3+.\" width=\"500\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;\" src=\"https://itsdrdan.github.io/textbook/figures/phone/fig-p597056-lewis-errors-phone.svg?v=20261113x\" />",
